<tt>HierarchicalSection</tt>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
        <div><a name="_standarddocument_2" id="_standarddocument_2"></a><h2>5.3<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>StandardDocument</h2><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2f092ef2-3a54-423a-a239-7656ed1d6b92" id="_2f092ef2-3a54-423a-a239-7656ed1d6b92"></a>The <i>StandardDocument</i> model is used to represent a standardization
document.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_cd097d3e-1168-4e21-a58a-a4e09e3c40e1" id="_cd097d3e-1168-4e21-a58a-a4e09e3c40e1"></a>Typically, a standardization document contains at least the
following data elements:</p>

<p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
Metadata information;
</p>
<p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
Clauses and subclauses;
</p>
<p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
Bibliographies;
</p>
<p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
Annexes if applicable.
</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ded836a7-f1a8-4386-b0c6-e9e25d169f4f" id="_ded836a7-f1a8-4386-b0c6-e9e25d169f4f"></a>The exact component requirements of a standardization document
can differ widely from one standardization body to the next.
Specialization is necessary to adopt the <tt>StandardDocument</tt>
model for such standardization bodies.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0c97e45a-e275-4fdc-952a-7acd0f54d19b" id="_0c97e45a-e275-4fdc-952a-7acd0f54d19b"></a>The <i>StandardDocument</i> model extends the <i>BasicDocument</i>
modelling of the document by requiring specific types
of sections.</p>
<p class="Tabletitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 3&#xA0;&#x2014; StandardDocument attributes</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;"><a name="_f5963c14-361e-46ce-9dfc-882a49d99957" id="_f5963c14-361e-46ce-9dfc-882a49d99957"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="center" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">Name</th><th valign="middle" align="center" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">Definition</th><th valign="middle" align="center" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">Mandatory/ Optional/ Conditional</th><th valign="middle" align="center" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">Max Occur</th><th valign="middle" align="center" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">Data Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">bibdata</td><td valign="top" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Bibliographic description of the document itself, expressed in the Relaton
