        <div><a name="_term_2" id="_term_2"></a><h2>9.8<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Term</h2><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_aa510275-5906-4c31-bb2d-c7bd69ab892c" id="_aa510275-5906-4c31-bb2d-c7bd69ab892c"></a>A term (<tt>Term</tt>) represents a terminology entry with
its definition.</p><div class="Note"><a name="_2ce53071-fed0-4308-91c1-165fda410aa4" id="_2ce53071-fed0-4308-91c1-165fda410aa4"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>The <tt>Term</tt> definition fully aligns with the structure
and requirements of terms in ISO/IEC DIR 2, 16.6.</p></div>

